// =============================================================================
// Brom Aleward — Innkeeper (THE QUEST HUB).  Questline: "Last Call" (vendor.inn)
// Keystone: the Hearthstone.  Teaches quest discovery + rest/respawn.
// Brom's Talk doubles as the RUMOR BOARD: it reads the per-vendor stage vars
// ($q_*_stage) and points the player at whatever vendor thread is still open,
// so the web self-advertises. Bridge-agnostic — no quest functions required.
// =============================================================================
title: TalkToInn
---
<<if $q_inn_stage == 0>>
    Brom: Pull up a chair. Every tale in Elarion passes through this hearth eventually.
    -> What's the word around the fire?
        <<jump RumorBoard>>
    -> Anything I can do for YOU, Brom?
        Brom: Now that you mention it — raiders have been casing the inn. Stay for the next surprise raid and help me hold the hearth?
        <<set $q_inn_stage = 1>>
        <<command: StartQuest vendor.inn>>
        Brom: "Last Call," the regulars are calling it. Don't let them burn my roof.
    -> Just rest a moment.
        Brom: Hearth's warm. Mind the door.
<<elseif $q_inn_stage == 1>>
    Brom: Are the raiders dealt with? My shutters can't take much more.
    -> The inn's safe.
        <<command: AdvanceQuest vendor.inn>>
        <<set $q_inn_stage = 2>>
        Brom: Hah! Drinks on the house. Stay on a while — I'll make this hearth your rally point. Fall in the field and you'll wake up right here.
    -> Not yet.
        Brom: Then keep your ale and your sword close, friend.
<<elseif $q_inn_stage == 2>>
    Brom: Shall I set the hearth as your rally and respawn point?
    -> Make it my home base.
        <<command: AdvanceQuest vendor.inn>>
        <<command: GiveKeystone "Hearthstone">>
        <<set $q_inn_stage = 9>>
        Brom: Done — the Hearthstone's yours. Fall anywhere, you wake here. <i>He leans in.</i> And listen... a traveler passed through, hooded, cold-eyed, asking after the Heart. Matched every tale of that Necromancer. He's real, and he's been here. Tell Alric.
    -> Not yet.
        Brom: The offer stands by the fire.
<<else>>
    Brom: The Hearthstone-keeper, welcome home. What'll it be?
    -> What's on the rumor board?
        <<jump RumorBoard>>
    -> Rest at the hearth.
        Brom: Always a bed for you here.
    -> Nothing tonight.
        Brom: Hearth's warm whenever you need it.
<<endif>>
===

// ── Rumor board: the soft quest log. Nudges the player toward whichever vendor
// thread is still open. Gates on the per-vendor stage vars ($q_*_stage: 0=unmet,
// 1..n=in progress, 9=bonded) so it is bridge-agnostic — needs no quest functions
// and works through ANY launch path (NPC station OR DialogueService). ──
title: RumorBoard
---
<<command: OpenRumorBoard>>
Brom: Here's the talk, then —
<<if $q_forge_stage > 0 and $q_forge_stage < 9>>
    Brom: Borin's forge is lit but his work's not done — he's still waiting on you.
<<elseif $q_forge_stage == 0>>
    Brom: Borin Emberhand's forge has gone cold. He's after a hand to relight it.
<<endif>>
<<if $q_armorer_stage > 0 and $q_armorer_stage < 9>>
    Brom: Dame Halvard's mid-job plating you — bring her what she asked.
<<elseif $q_armorer_stage == 0>>
    Brom: Dame Halvard mutters about salvage out past the wall. Coin in it, I'd wager.
<<endif>>
<<if $q_lumber_stage < 9>>
    Brom: Old Pell's grove's gone grey. He'd weep with thanks if you cleared the blight.
<<endif>>
<<if $q_granary_stage < 9>>
    Brom: Mother Wren's mill's idle. Empty bellies, she keeps saying.
<<endif>>
<<if $q_jeweler_stage < 9>>
    Brom: Sable Vey wants a flawless crystal — pays well, asks few questions. Maybe too few.
<<endif>>
<<if $q_market_stage < 9>>
    Brom: Coppin can't run his wagons — roads aren't safe. Glimmer for whoever clears them.
<<endif>>
<<if $q_stable_stage < 9>>
    Brom: Fenn Wildmane's beasts all bolted when the Heart dimmed. He'd teach you to tame one.
<<endif>>
Brom: And Warden Alric? He's the one who'll knit all this back into a fortress — when you've gathered the realm's crafts.
-> Thanks, Brom.
    Brom: Off you go. The hearth keeps.
===
